    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-5e",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "5E Serious contraventions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-5e"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, a serious contravention is a\ncontravention of a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory\nthat:\n\n(a) is a serious offence; or\n\n(b) is an offence punishable:\n\n(i) by imprisonment for a period, or a maximum period, of\nat least 3 years; or\n\n(ii) if the offence is committed by an individual—by a fine,\nor a maximum fine, of at least 180 penalty units; or\n\n(iii) if the offence cannot be committed by an individual—\nby a fine, or a maximum fine, of at least 900 penalty\nunits; or\n\n(c) could, if established, render the person committing the\ncontravention liable:\n\n(i) if the contravention were committed by an individual—\nto pay a pecuniary penalty of 180 penalty units or more,\n\nStored communications  Schedule 1\nPrincipal amendments  Part 1\n\nTelecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   5\nor to pay an amount that is the monetary equivalent of\n180 penalty units or more; or\n\n(ii) if the contravention cannot be committed by an\nindividual—to pay a pecuniary penalty of 900 penalty\nunits or more, or to pay an amount that is the monetary\nequivalent of 900 penalty units or more.\n\n(2) Except so far as the contrary intention appears, a contravention, or\na contravention of a particular kind, is taken, for the purposes of\nthis Act, to be a contravention, or to be a contravention of that\nkind, as the case may be, that:\n\n(a) has been committed or is being committed; or\n\n(b) is suspected on reasonable grounds of having been\ncommitted, of being committed or of being likely to be\ncommitted.\n\n(3) To avoid doubt, a reference in this section to a number of penalty\nunits in relation to a contravention of a law of a State or a Territory\nincludes a reference to an amount of a fine or pecuniary penalty\nthat is equivalent, under section 4AA of the Crimes Act 1914, to\nthat number of penalty units.\n5F  When a communication is passing over a telecommunications\nsystem\n\n(1) For the purposes of this Act, a communication:\n\n(a) is taken to start passing over a telecommunications system\nwhen it is sent or transmitted by the person sending the\ncommunication; and\n\n(b) is taken to continue to pass over the system until it becomes\naccessible to the intended recipient of the communication.\n\n(2) However, if a communication is sent from an address on a\ncomputer network operated by or on behalf of the Australian\nFederal Police, it is taken not to start passing over a\ntelecommunications system, for the purposes of this Act, until it is\nno longer under the control of any of the following:\n\n(a) any AFP employee responsible for operating, protecting and\nmaintaining the network;\n\n(b) any AFP employee responsible for enforcement of the\nprofessional standards of the Australian Federal Police.\n\nSchedule 1  Stored communications",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, a serious contravention is a\ncontravention of a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory\nthat:\n\n(a) is a serious offence; or\n\n(b) is an offence punishable:\n\n(i) by imprisonment for a period, or a maximum period, of\nat least 3 years; or\n\n(ii) if the offence is committed by an individual—by a fine,\nor a maximum fine, of at least 180 penalty units; or\n\n(iii) if the offence cannot be committed by an individual—\nby a fine, or a maximum fine, of at least 900 penalty\nunits; or\n\n(c) could, if established, render the person committing the\ncontravention liable:\n\n(i) if the contravention were committed by an individual—\nto pay a pecuniary penalty of 180 penalty units or more,\n\nStored communications  Schedule 1\nPrincipal amendments  Part 1\n\nTelecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   5\nor to pay an amount that is the monetary equivalent of\n180 penalty units or more; or\n\n(ii) if the contravention cannot be committed by an\nindividual—to pay a pecuniary penalty of 900 penalty\nunits or more, or to pay an amount that is the monetary\nequivalent of 900 penalty units or more.\n\n(2) Except so far as the contrary intention appears, a contravention, or\na contravention of a particular kind, is taken, for the purposes of\nthis Act, to be a contravention, or to be a contravention of that\nkind, as the case may be, that:\n\n(a) has been committed or is being committed; or\n\n(b) is suspected on reasonable grounds of having been\ncommitted, of being committed or of being likely to be\ncommitted.\n\n(3) To avoid doubt, a reference in this section to a number of penalty\nunits in relation to a contravention of a law of a State or a Territory\nincludes a reference to an amount of a fine or pecuniary penalty\nthat is equivalent, under section 4AA of the Crimes Act 1914, to\nthat number of penalty units.\n5F  When a communication is passing over a telecommunications\nsystem\n\n(1) For the purposes of this Act, a communication:\n\n(a) is taken to start ",
