      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.14",
      "values:originalText": "(4) In determining, for the purposes of paragraphs (2)(d) and (e),\nwhether an act or thing done by a person was reasonably necessary\nin order for the person to perform his or her duties effectively, a\ncourt is to have regard to such matters (if any) as are specified in,\nor ascertained in accordance with, the regulations.\nNote:\nThe civil remedy provisions in Part 3-7 may apply to a contravention\nof this section.\n\nSchedule 1  Stored communications",
      "skos:definition": "(4) In determining, for the purposes of paragraphs (2)(d) and (e),\nwhether an act or thing done by a person was reasonably necessary\nin order for the person to perform his or her duties effectively, a\ncourt is to have regard to such matters (if any) as are specified in,\nor ascertained in accordance with, the regulations.\nNote:\nThe civil remedy provisions in Part 3-7 may apply to a contravention\nof this section.\n\nSchedule 1  Stored communications",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-10"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-10-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-10-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "eb977632906a901bd334ef3b8c91a786949295acd19b5e9de467daad459926cb",
      "skos:note": "Court must consider regulations when determining reasonableness of actions."
    },
    {
