    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-110",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "110 Enforcement agencies may apply for stored communications",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-110"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.16",
      "values:originalText": "warrants\n\n(1) An enforcement agency may apply to an issuing authority for a\nstored communications warrant in respect of a person.\n\n(2) The application must be made on the agency’s behalf by:\n\n(a) if the agency is referred to in subsection 39(2)—a person\nreferred to in that subsection in relation to that agency; or\n\n(b) otherwise:\n\n(i) the chief officer of the agency; or\n\n(ii) an officer of the agency (by whatever name called) who\nholds, or is acting in, an office or position in the agency\nnominated under subsection (3).\n\n(3) The chief officer of the agency may, in writing, nominate for the\npurposes of subparagraph (2)(b)(ii) an office or position in the\nagency that is involved in the management of the agency.\n\n(4) A nomination under subsection (3) is not a legislative instrument.\n\nStored communications  Schedule 1\nPrincipal amendments  Part 1\n\nTelecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   13",
      "skos:definition": "warrants\n\n(1) An enforcement agency may apply to an issuing authority for a\nstored communications warrant in respect of a person.\n\n(2) The application must be made on the agency’s behalf by:\n\n(a) if the agency is referred to in subsection 39(2)—a person\nreferred to in that subsection in relation to that agency; or\n\n(b) otherwise:\n\n(i) the chief officer of the agency; or\n\n(ii) an officer of the agency (by whatever name called) who\nholds, or is acting in, an office or position in the agency\nnominated under subsection (3).\n\n(3) The chief officer of the agency may, in writing, nominate for the\npurposes of subparagraph (2)(b)(ii) an office or position in the\nagency that is involved in the management of the agency.\n\n(4) A nomination under subsection (3) is not a legislative instrument.\n\nStored communications  Schedule 1\nPrincipal amendments  Part 1\n\nTelecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   13",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-110-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-110-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-110-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-110-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6c4309c341e96053f5d26ad988867a9fd0938b074f54360d3e3a1ef12b1377fb"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-110",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "110 Enforcement agencies may apply for stored communications",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 16,
      "values:originalText": "warrants\n\n(1) An enforcement agency may apply to an issuing authority for a\nstored communications warrant in respect of a person.\n\n(2) The application must be made on the agency’s behalf by:\n\n(a) if the agency is referred to in subsection 39(2)—a person\nreferred to in that subsection in relation to that agency; or\n\n(b) otherwise:\n\n(i) the chief officer of the agency; or\n\n(ii) an officer of the agency (by whatever name called) who\nholds, or is acting in, an office or position in the agency\nnominated under subsection (3).\n\n(3) The chief officer of the agency may, in writing, nominate for the\npurposes of subparagraph (2)(b)(ii) an office or position in the\nagency that is involved in the management of the agency.\n\n(4) A nomination under subsection (3) is not a legislative instrument.\n\nStored communications  Schedule 1\nPrincipal amendments  Part 1\n\nTelecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   13"
    },
