    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-116-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "116(2) Issuing of stored communications warrants",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-116-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.18",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The matters to which the issuing authority must have regard are:\n\n(a) how much the privacy of any person or persons would be\nlikely to be interfered with by accessing those stored\ncommunications under a stored communications warrant; and\n\n(b) the gravity of the conduct constituting the serious\ncontravention; and\n\n(c) how much the information referred to in paragraph (1)(d)\nwould be likely to assist in connection with the investigation;\nand\n\n(d) to what extent methods of investigating the serious\ncontravention that do not involve the use of a stored\ncommunications warrant in relation to the person have been\nused by, or are available to, the agency; and\n\n(e) how much the use of such methods would be likely to assist\nin connection with the investigation by the agency of the\nserious contravention; and\n\n(f) how much the use of such methods would be likely to\nprejudice the investigation by the agency of the serious\ncontravention, whether because of delay or for any other\nreason.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The matters to which the issuing authority must have regard are:\n\n(a) how much the privacy of any person or persons would be\nlikely to be interfered with by accessing those stored\ncommunications under a stored communications warrant; and\n\n(b) the gravity of the conduct constituting the serious\ncontravention; and\n\n(c) how much the information referred to in paragraph (1)(d)\nwould be likely to assist in connection with the investigation;\nand\n\n(d) to what extent methods of investigating the serious\ncontravention that do not involve the use of a stored\ncommunications warrant in relation to the person have been\nused by, or are available to, the agency; and\n\n(e) how much the use of such methods would be likely to assist\nin connection with the investigation by the agency of the\nserious contravention; and\n\n(f) how much the use of such methods would be likely to\nprejudice the investigation by the agency of the serious\ncontravention, whether because of delay or for any other\nreason.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-116"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-116-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-116-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-116-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-116-ss-2-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-116-ss-2-logic-deontic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1ee7e3df313bef0160c1e8c4d91866858b5142578994efb3090bf61edfa9b674",
      "skos:note": "Authority must consider privacy impact and investigation methods when issuing stored communications warrants."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-116-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "116(2) Issuing of stored communications warrants",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 18,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The matters to which the issuing authority must have regard are:\n\n(a) how much the privacy of any person or persons would be\nlikely to be interfered with by accessing those stored\ncommunications under a stored communications warrant; and\n\n(b) the gravity of the conduct constituting the serious\ncontravention; and\n\n(c) how much the information referred to in paragraph (1)(d)\nwould be likely to assist in connection with the investigation;\nand\n\n(d) to what extent methods of investigating the serious\ncontravention that do not involve the use of a stored\ncommunications warrant in relation to the person have been\nused by, or are available to, the agency; and\n\n(e) how much the use of such methods would be likely to assist\nin connection with the investigation by the agency of the\nserious contravention; and\n\n(f) how much the use of such methods would be likely to\nprejudice the investigation by the agency of the serious\ncontravention, whether because of delay or for any other\nreason."
    },
