    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-121",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "121 What happens when stored communications warrants are",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-121"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "issued\n\nThe chief officer of the agency must cause:\n\n(a) the Managing Director of the carrier that holds the stored\ncommunications to which the warrant relates to be informed\nforthwith of the issue of the warrant; and\n\n(b) a copy of the warrant, certified in writing by a certifying\nofficer of the agency to be a true copy of the warrant, to be\ngiven as soon as practicable to the Managing Director of that\ncarrier.",
      "skos:definition": "issued\n\nThe chief officer of the agency must cause:\n\n(a) the Managing Director of the carrier that holds the stored\ncommunications to which the warrant relates to be informed\nforthwith of the issue of the warrant; and\n\n(b) a copy of the warrant, certified in writing by a certifying\nofficer of the agency to be a true copy of the warrant, to be\ngiven as soon as practicable to the Managing Director of that\ncarrier.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-121-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-121-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "10e1583dd6a35714505054c1a1e41b78f28e8c091ae5836268121a1a74b7a3c7",
      "skos:note": "Inform Managing Director of carrier about issued warrant and provide certified copy.",
      "dc:description": "true"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-121",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "121 What happens when stored communications warrants are",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 22,
      "values:originalText": "issued\n\nThe chief officer of the agency must cause:\n\n(a) the Managing Director of the carrier that holds the stored\ncommunications to which the warrant relates to be informed\nforthwith of the issue of the warrant; and\n\n(b) a copy of the warrant, certified in writing by a certifying\nofficer of the agency to be a true copy of the warrant, to be\ngiven as soon as practicable to the Managing Director of that\ncarrier."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-121-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-121"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-121-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Agency must inform carrier about warrant.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-122",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "122 Revocation of stored communications warrants by chief officers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-122"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The chief officer of an enforcement agency to which a stored\ncommunications warrant has been issued must, on being satisfied\nthat the grounds on which the warrant was issued have ceased to\nexist:\n\n(a) cause the chief officer of any other enforcement agency that\nis exercising authority under the warrant to be informed\nforthwith of the proposed revocation of the warrant; and\n\n(b) by writing signed by him or her, revoke the warrant.\n\nStored communications  Schedule 1\nPrincipal amendments  Part 1\n\nTelecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   19\n\n(2) The chief officer of an enforcement agency may at any time, by\nwriting signed by him or her, revoke a warrant issued to the agency\nafter causing the chief officer of any other enforcement agency that\nis exercising authority under the warrant to be informed forthwith\nthat the chief officer proposes to revoke the warrant.\n\n(3) The chief officer of an enforcement agency may delegate his or her\npower under subsection (2) to a certifying officer of the agency.\n\n(4) This section does not apply in relation to a warrant that has ceased\nto be in force.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The chief officer of an enforcement agency to which a stored\ncommunications warrant has been issued must, on being satisfied\nthat the grounds on which the warrant was issued have ceased to\nexist:\n\n(a) cause the chief officer of any other enforcement agency that\nis exercising authority under the warrant to be informed\nforthwith of the proposed revocation of the warrant; and\n\n(b) by writing signed by him or her, revoke the warrant.\n\nStored communications  Schedule 1\nPrincipal amendments  Part 1\n\nTelecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   19\n\n(2) The chief officer of an enforcement agency may at any time, by\nwriting signed by him or her, revoke a warrant issued to the agency\nafter causing the chief officer of any other enforcement agency that\nis exercising authority under the warrant to be informed forthwith\nthat the chief officer proposes to revoke the warrant.\n\n(3) The chief officer of an enforcement agency may delegate his or her\npower under subsection (2) to a certifying officer of the agency.\n\n(4) This section does not apply in relation to a warrant that has ceased\nto be in force.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-122-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-122-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-122-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-122-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2cecbdcc77ce66db1b9402a98f0db0da6d348afdb185edf1544de19203c5cb18"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-122",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "122 Revocation of stored communications warrants by chief officers",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 22,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The chief officer of an enforcement agency to which a stored\ncommunications warrant has been issued must, on being satisfied\nthat the grounds on which the warrant was issued have ceased to\nexist:\n\n(a) cause the chief officer of any other enforcement agency that\nis exercising authority under the warrant to be informed\nforthwith of the proposed revocation of the warrant; and\n\n(b) by writing signed by him or her, revoke the warrant.\n\nStored communications  Schedule 1\nPrincipal amendments  Part 1\n\nTelecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   19\n\n(2) The chief officer of an enforcement agency may at any time, by\nwriting signed by him or her, revoke a warrant issued to the agency\nafter causing the chief officer of any other enforcement agency that\nis exercising authority under the warrant to be informed forthwith\nthat the chief officer proposes to revoke the warrant.\n\n(3) The chief officer of an enforcement agency may delegate his or her\npower under subsection (2) to a certifying officer of the agency.\n\n(4) This section does not apply in relation to a warrant that has ceased\nto be in force."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-122-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "122(1) Revocation of stored communications warrants by chief officers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-122-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
