      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The chief officer of an enforcement agency to which a stored\ncommunications warrant has been issued must, on being satisfied\nthat the grounds on which the warrant was issued have ceased to\nexist:\n\n(a) cause the chief officer of any other enforcement agency that\nis exercising authority under the warrant to be informed\nforthwith of the proposed revocation of the warrant; and\n\n(b) by writing signed by him or her, revoke the warrant.\n\nStored communications  Schedule 1\nPrincipal amendments  Part 1\n\nTelecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   19",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The chief officer of an enforcement agency to which a stored\ncommunications warrant has been issued must, on being satisfied\nthat the grounds on which the warrant was issued have ceased to\nexist:\n\n(a) cause the chief officer of any other enforcement agency that\nis exercising authority under the warrant to be informed\nforthwith of the proposed revocation of the warrant; and\n\n(b) by writing signed by him or her, revoke the warrant.\n\nStored communications  Schedule 1\nPrincipal amendments  Part 1\n\nTelecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   19",
      "values:partOf": {
