    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-122-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "122(2) Revocation of stored communications warrants by chief officers",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 22,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The chief officer of an enforcement agency may at any time, by\nwriting signed by him or her, revoke a warrant issued to the agency\nafter causing the chief officer of any other enforcement agency that\nis exercising authority under the warrant to be informed forthwith\nthat the chief officer proposes to revoke the warrant."
    },
    {
