      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.23",
      "values:originalText": "communications warrants\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) the Managing Director of a carrier has been informed, under\nsection 121, of the issue of a stored communications warrant;\nand\n\n(b) it is proposed, under the warrant, to access stored\ncommunications that, immediately before they became stored\ncommunications, had passed over a telecommunications\nservice operated by a carrier; and\n\nSchedule 1  Stored communications",
      "skos:definition": "communications warrants\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) the Managing Director of a carrier has been informed, under\nsection 121, of the issue of a stored communications warrant;\nand\n\n(b) it is proposed, under the warrant, to access stored\ncommunications that, immediately before they became stored\ncommunications, had passed over a telecommunications\nservice operated by a carrier; and\n\nSchedule 1  Stored communications",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-124-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-124-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
