    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-20",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20 Telecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-20"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "(c) the service was not identified in the warrant;\nthe chief officer must cause the Managing Director of the carrier to\nbe given, as soon as practicable, a description in writing of the\nservice sufficient to identify it.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) the Managing Director of a carrier has been informed, under\nsubsection (1) of the issue of a stored communications\nwarrant; and\n\n(b) the chief officer of the agency to which the warrant was\nissued, or a certifying officer of that agency, is satisfied that\nit is no longer necessary to access stored communications\nthat, immediately before they became stored\ncommunications, had passed over that service;\nthe chief officer or the certifying officer must cause:\n\n(c) the Managing Director to be informed forthwith of the fact;\nand\n\n(d) confirmation in writing of the fact to be given as soon as\npracticable to the Managing Director.",
      "skos:definition": "(c) the service was not identified in the warrant;\nthe chief officer must cause the Managing Director of the carrier to\nbe given, as soon as practicable, a description in writing of the\nservice sufficient to identify it.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) the Managing Director of a carrier has been informed, under\nsubsection (1) of the issue of a stored communications\nwarrant; and\n\n(b) the chief officer of the agency to which the warrant was\nissued, or a certifying officer of that agency, is satisfied that\nit is no longer necessary to access stored communications\nthat, immediately before they became stored\ncommunications, had passed over that service;\nthe chief officer or the certifying officer must cause:\n\n(c) the Managing Director to be informed forthwith of the fact;\nand\n\n(d) confirmation in writing of the fact to be given as soon as\npracticable to the Managing Director.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-20-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-20-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6b8657b6c84d1124a182ba141f4b653f52304f81bfc2edac4fd5d87e8c20eee2",
      "skos:note": "Chief officer must inform Managing Director of carrier about changes in service identification.",
      "dc:description": "Confirmation in writing"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-20",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20 Telecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 24,
      "values:originalText": "(c) the service was not identified in the warrant;\nthe chief officer must cause the Managing Director of the carrier to\nbe given, as soon as practicable, a description in writing of the\nservice sufficient to identify it.\n\n(2) If:\n\n(a) the Managing Director of a carrier has been informed, under\nsubsection (1) of the issue of a stored communications\nwarrant; and\n\n(b) the chief officer of the agency to which the warrant was\nissued, or a certifying officer of that agency, is satisfied that\nit is no longer necessary to access stored communications\nthat, immediately before they became stored\ncommunications, had passed over that service;\nthe chief officer or the certifying officer must cause:\n\n(c) the Managing Director to be informed forthwith of the fact;\nand\n\n(d) confirmation in writing of the fact to be given as soon as\npracticable to the Managing Director."
    },
