      "cml:conclusionText": "Access to stored communications"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-127",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "127 Exercise of authority conferred by warrant",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-127"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The authority conferred by a stored communications warrant must\nnot be exercised by a person who is not an officer or staff member\nof an enforcement agency in relation to whom an approval under\nsubsection (2) is in force in relation to the warrant.\n\nStored communications  Schedule 1\nPrincipal amendments  Part 1\n\nTelecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   21\n\n(2) The chief officer of an agency, or an officer of an agency in\nrelation to whom an appointment under subsection (3) is in force,\nmay approve any of the following to exercise the authority\nconferred by warrants, or classes of warrants, issued to the agency:\n\n(a) officers or staff members of the agency;\n\n(b) classes of officers or staff members of the agency;\n\n(c) officers or staff members of another enforcement agency;\n\n(d) classes of officers or staff members of another enforcement\nagency.\n\n(3) The chief officer of an enforcement agency may appoint in writing\nan officer of the agency to be an approving officer for the purposes\nof subsection (2).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The authority conferred by a stored communications warrant must\nnot be exercised by a person who is not an officer or staff member\nof an enforcement agency in relation to whom an approval under\nsubsection (2) is in force in relation to the warrant.\n\nStored communications  Schedule 1\nPrincipal amendments  Part 1\n\nTelecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   21\n\n(2) The chief officer of an agency, or an officer of an agency in\nrelation to whom an appointment under subsection (3) is in force,\nmay approve any of the following to exercise the authority\nconferred by warrants, or classes of warrants, issued to the agency:\n\n(a) officers or staff members of the agency;\n\n(b) classes of officers or staff members of the agency;\n\n(c) officers or staff members of another enforcement agency;\n\n(d) classes of officers or staff members of another enforcement\nagency.\n\n(3) The chief officer of an enforcement agency may appoint in writing\nan officer of the agency to be an approving officer for the purposes\nof subsection (2).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-127-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-127-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-127-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bea55b00b47eeef2dbec834687a4e145d49a734b0963e17b1695b1116c3ca7af"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-127",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "127 Exercise of authority conferred by warrant",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 24,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The authority conferred by a stored communications warrant must\nnot be exercised by a person who is not an officer or staff member\nof an enforcement agency in relation to whom an approval under\nsubsection (2) is in force in relation to the warrant.\n\nStored communications  Schedule 1\nPrincipal amendments  Part 1\n\nTelecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   21\n\n(2) The chief officer of an agency, or an officer of an agency in\nrelation to whom an appointment under subsection (3) is in force,\nmay approve any of the following to exercise the authority\nconferred by warrants, or classes of warrants, issued to the agency:\n\n(a) officers or staff members of the agency;\n\n(b) classes of officers or staff members of the agency;\n\n(c) officers or staff members of another enforcement agency;\n\n(d) classes of officers or staff members of another enforcement\nagency.\n\n(3) The chief officer of an enforcement agency may appoint in writing\nan officer of the agency to be an approving officer for the purposes\nof subsection (2)."
    },
