      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The chief officer of an agency, or an officer of an agency in\nrelation to whom an appointment under subsection (3) is in force,\nmay approve any of the following to exercise the authority\nconferred by warrants, or classes of warrants, issued to the agency:\n\n(a) officers or staff members of the agency;\n\n(b) classes of officers or staff members of the agency;\n\n(c) officers or staff members of another enforcement agency;\n\n(d) classes of officers or staff members of another enforcement\nagency.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The chief officer of an agency, or an officer of an agency in\nrelation to whom an appointment under subsection (3) is in force,\nmay approve any of the following to exercise the authority\nconferred by warrants, or classes of warrants, issued to the agency:\n\n(a) officers or staff members of the agency;\n\n(b) classes of officers or staff members of the agency;\n\n(c) officers or staff members of another enforcement agency;\n\n(d) classes of officers or staff members of another enforcement\nagency.",
