    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-129",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "129 Evidentiary certificates relating to actions by carriers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-129"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.26",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Managing Director or secretary of:\n\n(a) a carrier; or\n\n(b) a body corporate of which the carrier is a subsidiary;\nmay issue a written certificate signed by him or her setting out such\nfacts as he or she considers relevant with respect to acts or things\ndone by, or in relation to, employees of the carrier in order to\nenable a warrant to be executed.\n\n(2) A document purporting to be a certificate issued under\nsubsection (1) and purporting to be signed by the Managing\nDirector or secretary of a carrier, or of a body corporate of which\nthe carrier is a subsidiary:\n\n(a) is to be received in evidence in an exempt proceeding\nwithout further proof; and\n\n(b) in an exempt proceeding, is conclusive evidence of the\nmatters stated in the document.\n\n(3) For the purposes of this section, the question whether a body\ncorporate is a subsidiary of another body corporate is to be\ndetermined in the same manner as the question is determined under\nthe Corporations Act 2001.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Managing Director or secretary of:\n\n(a) a carrier; or\n\n(b) a body corporate of which the carrier is a subsidiary;\nmay issue a written certificate signed by him or her setting out such\nfacts as he or she considers relevant with respect to acts or things\ndone by, or in relation to, employees of the carrier in order to\nenable a warrant to be executed.\n\n(2) A document purporting to be a certificate issued under\nsubsection (1) and purporting to be signed by the Managing\nDirector or secretary of a carrier, or of a body corporate of which\nthe carrier is a subsidiary:\n\n(a) is to be received in evidence in an exempt proceeding\nwithout further proof; and\n\n(b) in an exempt proceeding, is conclusive evidence of the\nmatters stated in the document.\n\n(3) For the purposes of this section, the question whether a body\ncorporate is a subsidiary of another body corporate is to be\ndetermined in the same manner as the question is determined under\nthe Corporations Act 2001.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-129-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-129-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-129-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5e5cc8b2a7f1f2b42a28ec1d2596fcd623085e2a239bd59054a2ddbf7d6bb8a1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-129",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "129 Evidentiary certificates relating to actions by carriers",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 26,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Managing Director or secretary of:\n\n(a) a carrier; or\n\n(b) a body corporate of which the carrier is a subsidiary;\nmay issue a written certificate signed by him or her setting out such\nfacts as he or she considers relevant with respect to acts or things\ndone by, or in relation to, employees of the carrier in order to\nenable a warrant to be executed.\n\n(2) A document purporting to be a certificate issued under\nsubsection (1) and purporting to be signed by the Managing\nDirector or secretary of a carrier, or of a body corporate of which\nthe carrier is a subsidiary:\n\n(a) is to be received in evidence in an exempt proceeding\nwithout further proof; and\n\n(b) in an exempt proceeding, is conclusive evidence of the\nmatters stated in the document.\n\n(3) For the purposes of this section, the question whether a body\ncorporate is a subsidiary of another body corporate is to be\ndetermined in the same manner as the question is determined under\nthe Corporations Act 2001."
    },
