      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "(iii) makes a record of information; or\n\n(iv) gives information in evidence in a proceeding; and\n\n(b) the information is:\n\n(i) lawfully accessed information; or\n\n(ii) information obtained by accessing a stored\ncommunication in contravention of subsection 108(1);\nor\n\n(iii) stored communications warrant information.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years or 120 penalty units, or both.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to conduct permitted under this Part.\nNote 1:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).\nNote 2:\nThe civil remedy provisions in Part 3-7 may apply to a contravention\nof this section.",
      "skos:definition": "(iii) makes a record of information; or\n\n(iv) gives information in evidence in a proceeding; and\n\n(b) the information is:\n\n(i) lawfully accessed information; or\n\n(ii) information obtained by accessing a stored\ncommunication in contravention of subsection 108(1);\nor\n\n(iii) stored communications warrant information.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years or 120 penalty units, or both.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to conduct permitted under this Part.\nNote 1:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).\nNote 2:\nThe civil remedy provisions in Part 3-7 may apply to a contravention\nof this section.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-24-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-24-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-24-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-24-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-24-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-24-logic-diffusion-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6dc8e9c4f7029d242ea2b3c8e92cbf9d8ce39bc028dfd1018b0b09f105cf526a",
      "skos:note": "Making or giving information in evidence without lawful access is prohibited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-24",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "24 Telecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 28,
      "values:originalText": "(iii) makes a record of information; or\n\n(iv) gives information in evidence in a proceeding; and\n\n(b) the information is:\n\n(i) lawfully accessed information; or\n\n(ii) information obtained by accessing a stored\ncommunication in contravention of subsection 108(1);\nor\n\n(iii) stored communications warrant information.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years or 120 penalty units, or both.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to conduct permitted under this Part.\nNote 1:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).\nNote 2:\nThe civil remedy provisions in Part 3-7 may apply to a contravention\nof this section."
    },
