    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-136",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "136 Dealing in connection with Organisation’s functions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-136"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.30",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person may, in connection with the performance by the\nOrganisation of its functions, or otherwise for purposes of security,\ncommunicate to another person, make use of, or make a record of\nthe following:\n\n(a) lawfully accessed information other than foreign intelligence\ninformation;\n\n(b) stored communications warrant information.\n\n(2) The Director-General of Security may, in connection with the\nperformance by the Organisation of its functions, communicate\nforeign intelligence information to an officer or employee of the\nOrganisation.\n\n(3) An officer or employee of the Organisation may, in connection\nwith the performance by the Organisation of its functions,\ncommunicate foreign intelligence information to the\nDirector-General of Security or to another such officer or\nemployee.\n\n(4) The Director-General of Security or an officer or employee of the\nOrganisation may, in connection with the performance by the\nOrganisation of its functions, make use of, or make a record of,\nforeign intelligence information.\n\nStored communications  Schedule 1\nPrincipal amendments  Part 1\n\nTelecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   27",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person may, in connection with the performance by the\nOrganisation of its functions, or otherwise for purposes of security,\ncommunicate to another person, make use of, or make a record of\nthe following:\n\n(a) lawfully accessed information other than foreign intelligence\ninformation;\n\n(b) stored communications warrant information.\n\n(2) The Director-General of Security may, in connection with the\nperformance by the Organisation of its functions, communicate\nforeign intelligence information to an officer or employee of the\nOrganisation.\n\n(3) An officer or employee of the Organisation may, in connection\nwith the performance by the Organisation of its functions,\ncommunicate foreign intelligence information to the\nDirector-General of Security or to another such officer or\nemployee.\n\n(4) The Director-General of Security or an officer or employee of the\nOrganisation may, in connection with the performance by the\nOrganisation of its functions, make use of, or make a record of,\nforeign intelligence information.\n\nStored communications  Schedule 1\nPrincipal amendments  Part 1\n\nTelecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   27",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-136-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-136-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-136-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-136-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "22110b330f00bea35aae19b9883b3b04fdb6e7870706c244fcf66657ab10b530"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-136",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "136 Dealing in connection with Organisation’s functions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 30,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person may, in connection with the performance by the\nOrganisation of its functions, or otherwise for purposes of security,\ncommunicate to another person, make use of, or make a record of\nthe following:\n\n(a) lawfully accessed information other than foreign intelligence\ninformation;\n\n(b) stored communications warrant information.\n\n(2) The Director-General of Security may, in connection with the\nperformance by the Organisation of its functions, communicate\nforeign intelligence information to an officer or employee of the\nOrganisation.\n\n(3) An officer or employee of the Organisation may, in connection\nwith the performance by the Organisation of its functions,\ncommunicate foreign intelligence information to the\nDirector-General of Security or to another such officer or\nemployee.\n\n(4) The Director-General of Security or an officer or employee of the\nOrganisation may, in connection with the performance by the\nOrganisation of its functions, make use of, or make a record of,\nforeign intelligence information.\n\nStored communications  Schedule 1\nPrincipal amendments  Part 1\n\nTelecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   27"
    },
