    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-137",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "137 Communicating information obtained by Organisation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-137"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.31",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Director-General of Security may, in accordance with\nparagraph 18(3)(a) or (b) of the Australian Security Intelligence\nOrganisation Act 1979, communicate the following to another\nperson:\n\n(a) lawfully accessed information;\n\n(b) stored communications warrant information.\n\n(2) The communication may be made by the Director-General of\nSecurity personally or by a person authorised by the\nDirector-General.\n\n(3) A person to whom foreign intelligence information has been\ncommunicated:\n\n(a) in accordance with subsection (1); or\n\n(b) in accordance with an approval given under this subsection;\nmay communicate that information to such persons, and in such\nmanner, as are approved in writing by the Attorney-General.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Director-General of Security may, in accordance with\nparagraph 18(3)(a) or (b) of the Australian Security Intelligence\nOrganisation Act 1979, communicate the following to another\nperson:\n\n(a) lawfully accessed information;\n\n(b) stored communications warrant information.\n\n(2) The communication may be made by the Director-General of\nSecurity personally or by a person authorised by the\nDirector-General.\n\n(3) A person to whom foreign intelligence information has been\ncommunicated:\n\n(a) in accordance with subsection (1); or\n\n(b) in accordance with an approval given under this subsection;\nmay communicate that information to such persons, and in such\nmanner, as are approved in writing by the Attorney-General.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-137-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-137-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-137-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bb31f3c54bc17b6f1b2fa0f8bfd58835c6fdfe9a27e042dddc1a0d92a11526cb"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-137",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "137 Communicating information obtained by Organisation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 31,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Director-General of Security may, in accordance with\nparagraph 18(3)(a) or (b) of the Australian Security Intelligence\nOrganisation Act 1979, communicate the following to another\nperson:\n\n(a) lawfully accessed information;\n\n(b) stored communications warrant information.\n\n(2) The communication may be made by the Director-General of\nSecurity personally or by a person authorised by the\nDirector-General.\n\n(3) A person to whom foreign intelligence information has been\ncommunicated:\n\n(a) in accordance with subsection (1); or\n\n(b) in accordance with an approval given under this subsection;\nmay communicate that information to such persons, and in such\nmanner, as are approved in writing by the Attorney-General."
    },
