    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-150",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "150 Destruction of records",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-150"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.37",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) information, or a record, that was obtained by accessing a\nstored communication (whether or not in contravention of\nsubsection 108(1)) is in an enforcement agency’s possession;\nand\n\n(b) the chief officer of the agency is satisfied that the information\nor record is not likely to be required for a purpose referred to\nin subsection 139(2);\nthe chief officer must cause the information or record to be\ndestroyed forthwith.\n\nSchedule 1  Stored communications",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n\n(a) information, or a record, that was obtained by accessing a\nstored communication (whether or not in contravention of\nsubsection 108(1)) is in an enforcement agency’s possession;\nand\n\n(b) the chief officer of the agency is satisfied that the information\nor record is not likely to be required for a purpose referred to\nin subsection 139(2);\nthe chief officer must cause the information or record to be\ndestroyed forthwith.\n\nSchedule 1  Stored communications",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-150-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-150-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-150-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-150-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-150-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-150-logic-cogai-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "67e465a2dfcb0a701d1940fddf25128f67de77b9bf1bdb304d1816031cee7fda",
      "skos:note": "Destroy stored communications if not required for a purpose."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-150",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "150 Destruction of records",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 37,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n(a) information, or a record, that was obtained by accessing a\nstored communication (whether or not in contravention of\nsubsection 108(1)) is in an enforcement agency’s possession;\nand\n\n(b) the chief officer of the agency is satisfied that the information\nor record is not likely to be required for a purpose referred to\nin subsection 139(2);\nthe chief officer must cause the information or record to be\ndestroyed forthwith.\n\nSchedule 1  Stored communications"
    },
