    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-151",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "151 Enforcement agencies to keep documents connected with issue",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-151"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.38",
      "values:originalText": "of warrants\n\nThe chief officer of an enforcement agency must cause to be kept\nin the agency’s records:\n\n(a) each stored communications warrant issued to the agency;\nand\n\n(b) each instrument revoking such a warrant; and\n\n(c) a copy of each certificate issued under subsection 130(1) by a\ncertifying officer of the agency; and\n\n(d) each authorisation by the chief officer under subsection\n135(2); and\n\n(e) particulars of the destruction of information and records that\nthe chief officer has caused in accordance with section 150.",
      "skos:definition": "of warrants\n\nThe chief officer of an enforcement agency must cause to be kept\nin the agency’s records:\n\n(a) each stored communications warrant issued to the agency;\nand\n\n(b) each instrument revoking such a warrant; and\n\n(c) a copy of each certificate issued under subsection 130(1) by a\ncertifying officer of the agency; and\n\n(d) each authorisation by the chief officer under subsection\n135(2); and\n\n(e) particulars of the destruction of information and records that\nthe chief officer has caused in accordance with section 150.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-151-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-151-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "14b16c0260903750eb9d5d0eba29c793616ffc07e764caace4bb71b2eff6ddfd",
      "skos:note": "Enforcement agency must keep documents connected with issue.",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-151",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "151 Enforcement agencies to keep documents connected with issue",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 38,
      "values:originalText": "of warrants\n\nThe chief officer of an enforcement agency must cause to be kept\nin the agency’s records:\n\n(a) each stored communications warrant issued to the agency;\nand\n\n(b) each instrument revoking such a warrant; and\n\n(c) a copy of each certificate issued under subsection 130(1) by a\ncertifying officer of the agency; and\n\n(d) each authorisation by the chief officer under subsection\n135(2); and\n\n(e) particulars of the destruction of information and records that\nthe chief officer has caused in accordance with section 150."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-151-norm",
