    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-152",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "152 Functions of Ombudsman",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-152"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.38",
      "values:originalText": "Subject to this Division, the Ombudsman has the following\nadditional functions:\n\n(a) to inspect an enforcement agency’s records in order to\nascertain, so far as is practicable, the extent of compliance, in\nrelation to those records, with sections 150 and 151; and\n\n(b) to report to the Minister about the results of inspections under\nthis Division; and\n\n(c) to do anything incidental or conducive to the performance of\nany of the preceding functions.\n\nStored communications  Schedule 1\nPrincipal amendments  Part 1\n\nTelecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   35",
      "skos:definition": "Subject to this Division, the Ombudsman has the following\nadditional functions:\n\n(a) to inspect an enforcement agency’s records in order to\nascertain, so far as is practicable, the extent of compliance, in\nrelation to those records, with sections 150 and 151; and\n\n(b) to report to the Minister about the results of inspections under\nthis Division; and\n\n(c) to do anything incidental or conducive to the performance of\nany of the preceding functions.\n\nStored communications  Schedule 1\nPrincipal amendments  Part 1\n\nTelecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   35",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-152-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-152-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "794adb6d1ad2c45c54ff0556820dac6677c61f26d7ca927cdedbfc4a93a714c8",
      "skos:note": "Inspect enforcement agency records to ascertain compliance with sections 150 and 151."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-152",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "152 Functions of Ombudsman",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 38,
      "values:originalText": "Subject to this Division, the Ombudsman has the following\nadditional functions:\n\n(a) to inspect an enforcement agency’s records in order to\nascertain, so far as is practicable, the extent of compliance, in\nrelation to those records, with sections 150 and 151; and\n\n(b) to report to the Minister about the results of inspections under\nthis Division; and\n\n(c) to do anything incidental or conducive to the performance of\nany of the preceding functions.\n\nStored communications  Schedule 1\nPrincipal amendments  Part 1\n\nTelecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   35"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-152-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-152"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-152-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "has",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to inspect records",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-153",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "153 Reports",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-153"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.39",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Ombudsman must report to the Minister in writing, in relation\nto each enforcement agency, about the results of the inspections\nunder section 152, during that financial year, of the agency’s\nrecords.\n\n(2) Each report under subsection (1) in relation to a financial year must\nbe given to the Minister as soon as practicable after the end of the\nfinancial year, and in any event within 3 months after the end of\nthe financial year.\n\n(3) If, as a result of an inspection under this Division of the records of\nan enforcement agency, the Ombudsman is of the opinion that an\nofficer of the agency has contravened a provision of this Act (other\nthan section 150 or 151), the Ombudsman may include in his or her\nreport on the inspection a report on the contravention.\nNote:\nIn complying with this section, the Ombudsman remains bound by the\nobligations imposed by section 133 relating to disclosure of accessed\ninformation or stored communications warrant information.\n\n(4) The Ombudsman may report to the Minister in writing at any time\nabout the results of an inspection under this Division and must do\nso if so requested by the Minister.\n\n(5) The Ombudsman must give a copy of a report under subsection (1)\nor (3) to the chief officer of the enforcement agency to which the\nreport relates.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Ombudsman must report to the Minister in writing, in relation\nto each enforcement agency, about the results of the inspections\nunder section 152, during that financial year, of the agency’s\nrecords.\n\n(2) Each report under subsection (1) in relation to a financial year must\nbe given to the Minister as soon as practicable after the end of the\nfinancial year, and in any event within 3 months after the end of\nthe financial year.\n\n(3) If, as a result of an inspection under this Division of the records of\nan enforcement agency, the Ombudsman is of the opinion that an\nofficer of the agency has contravened a provision of this Act (other\nthan section 150 or 151), the Ombudsman may include in his or her\nreport on the inspection a report on the contravention.\nNote:\nIn complying with this section, the Ombudsman remains bound by the\nobligations imposed by section 133 relating to disclosure of accessed\ninformation or stored communications warrant information.\n\n(4) The Ombudsman may report to the Minister in writing at any time\nabout the results of an inspection under this Division and must do\nso if so requested by the Minister.\n\n(5) The Ombudsman must give a copy of a report under subsection (1)\nor (3) to the chief officer of the enforcement agency to which the\nreport relates.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-153-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-153-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-153-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-153-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-153-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d0c45832500daeb50bc27ef4b720a1a946f1cc3a592f5b9398b27b48e019afd4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-153",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "153 Reports",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 39,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Ombudsman must report to the Minister in writing, in relation\nto each enforcement agency, about the results of the inspections\nunder section 152, during that financial year, of the agency’s\nrecords.\n\n(2) Each report under subsection (1) in relation to a financial year must\nbe given to the Minister as soon as practicable after the end of the\nfinancial year, and in any event within 3 months after the end of\nthe financial year.\n\n(3) If, as a result of an inspection under this Division of the records of\nan enforcement agency, the Ombudsman is of the opinion that an\nofficer of the agency has contravened a provision of this Act (other\nthan section 150 or 151), the Ombudsman may include in his or her\nreport on the inspection a report on the contravention.\nNote:\nIn complying with this section, the Ombudsman remains bound by the\nobligations imposed by section 133 relating to disclosure of accessed\ninformation or stored communications warrant information.\n\n(4) The Ombudsman may report to the Minister in writing at any time\nabout the results of an inspection under this Division and must do\nso if so requested by the Minister.\n\n(5) The Ombudsman must give a copy of a report under subsection (1)\nor (3) to the chief officer of the enforcement agency to which the\nreport relates."
    },
    {
