    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-153-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "153(3) Reports",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-153-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.39",
      "values:originalText": "(3) If, as a result of an inspection under this Division of the records of\nan enforcement agency, the Ombudsman is of the opinion that an\nofficer of the agency has contravened a provision of this Act (other\nthan section 150 or 151), the Ombudsman may include in his or her\nreport on the inspection a report on the contravention.\nNote:\nIn complying with this section, the Ombudsman remains bound by the\nobligations imposed by section 133 relating to disclosure of accessed\ninformation or stored communications warrant information.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) If, as a result of an inspection under this Division of the records of\nan enforcement agency, the Ombudsman is of the opinion that an\nofficer of the agency has contravened a provision of this Act (other\nthan section 150 or 151), the Ombudsman may include in his or her\nreport on the inspection a report on the contravention.\nNote:\nIn complying with this section, the Ombudsman remains bound by the\nobligations imposed by section 133 relating to disclosure of accessed\ninformation or stored communications warrant information.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-153"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-153-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-153-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7cec9e4c07044cc04dd47a229fde7db5beff56f250c7d9c3aea69b6068829457",
      "skos:note": "Ombudsman may report contravention of Act provision"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-153-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "153(3) Reports",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 39,
      "values:originalText": "(3) If, as a result of an inspection under this Division of the records of\nan enforcement agency, the Ombudsman is of the opinion that an\nofficer of the agency has contravened a provision of this Act (other\nthan section 150 or 151), the Ombudsman may include in his or her\nreport on the inspection a report on the contravention.\nNote:\nIn complying with this section, the Ombudsman remains bound by the\nobligations imposed by section 133 relating to disclosure of accessed\ninformation or stored communications warrant information."
    },
