    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-36",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "36 Telecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-36"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.40",
      "values:originalText": "(a) giving information to an inspecting officer (whether orally or\nin writing and whether or not in answer to a question); or\n\n(b) giving to an inspecting officer access to a record of the\nagency;\nfor the purposes of an inspection under this Part of the agency’s\nrecords.\n\n(2) Neither section 133 nor any other law prevents an officer of an\nenforcement agency from making a record of information, or\ncausing a record of information to be made, for the purposes of\ngiving the information to a person as permitted by subsection (1).",
      "skos:definition": "(a) giving information to an inspecting officer (whether orally or\nin writing and whether or not in answer to a question); or\n\n(b) giving to an inspecting officer access to a record of the\nagency;\nfor the purposes of an inspection under this Part of the agency’s\nrecords.\n\n(2) Neither section 133 nor any other law prevents an officer of an\nenforcement agency from making a record of information, or\ncausing a record of information to be made, for the purposes of\ngiving the information to a person as permitted by subsection (1).",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-36-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-36-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0ad02fc343402c934341ced0d6e71d0b69c152bc1edfc2d7204ea8db9c09b1bd",
      "skos:note": "Giving information to an inspecting officer and access to agency records for inspection purposes."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-36",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "36 Telecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 40,
      "values:originalText": "(a) giving information to an inspecting officer (whether orally or\nin writing and whether or not in answer to a question); or\n\n(b) giving to an inspecting officer access to a record of the\nagency;\nfor the purposes of an inspection under this Part of the agency’s\nrecords.\n\n(2) Neither section 133 nor any other law prevents an officer of an\nenforcement agency from making a record of information, or\ncausing a record of information to be made, for the purposes of\ngiving the information to a person as permitted by subsection (1)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-36-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-36"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-36-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "OBLIGES",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Imposes a duty on the agency to provide information and access records.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-156",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "156 Dealing with information for the purposes of inspection and",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-156"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.40",
      "values:originalText": "report\n\n(1) An inspecting officer may communicate to another inspecting\nofficer, make use of, or make a record of, information for the\npurposes of an inspection (or of a report on an inspection) under\nthis Division of an enforcement agency’s records if:\n\n(a) the information was given or communicated to the inspecting\nofficer, as permitted by subsection 155(1) or this section, for\nthe purposes of an inspection (or of a report on an inspection)\nunder this Division of an enforcement agency’s records; or\n\n(b) the inspecting officer obtained the information as a result of\nbeing given access to records of an enforcement agency, as\npermitted by subsection 155(1), for the purposes of an\ninspection under this Division of the agency’s records.\n\n(2) This section has effect despite section 133 or any other law.",
      "skos:definition": "report\n\n(1) An inspecting officer may communicate to another inspecting\nofficer, make use of, or make a record of, information for the\npurposes of an inspection (or of a report on an inspection) under\nthis Division of an enforcement agency’s records if:\n\n(a) the information was given or communicated to the inspecting\nofficer, as permitted by subsection 155(1) or this section, for\nthe purposes of an inspection (or of a report on an inspection)\nunder this Division of an enforcement agency’s records; or\n\n(b) the inspecting officer obtained the information as a result of\nbeing given access to records of an enforcement agency, as\npermitted by subsection 155(1), for the purposes of an\ninspection under this Division of the agency’s records.\n\n(2) This section has effect despite section 133 or any other law.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-156-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-156-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "845e91831319e89c4d656bdb80c278ac09a7230d61e5dfd2e1b1fbb436ac8917"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-156",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "156 Dealing with information for the purposes of inspection and",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 40,
      "values:originalText": "report\n\n(1) An inspecting officer may communicate to another inspecting\nofficer, make use of, or make a record of, information for the\npurposes of an inspection (or of a report on an inspection) under\nthis Division of an enforcement agency’s records if:\n\n(a) the information was given or communicated to the inspecting\nofficer, as permitted by subsection 155(1) or this section, for\nthe purposes of an inspection (or of a report on an inspection)\nunder this Division of an enforcement agency’s records; or\n\n(b) the inspecting officer obtained the information as a result of\nbeing given access to records of an enforcement agency, as\npermitted by subsection 155(1), for the purposes of an\ninspection under this Division of the agency’s records.\n\n(2) This section has effect despite section 133 or any other law."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-156-ss-1",
