    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-157",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "157 Application of Ombudsman Act",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-157"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.40",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Section 11A of the Ombudsman Act 1976 does not apply in\nrelation to the exercise or proposed exercise of a power, or the\nperformance or the proposed performance of a function, of the\nOmbudsman under this Division.\n\n(2) A reference in section 19 of the Ombudsman Act 1976 to the\nOmbudsman’s operations does not include a reference to anything\nthat an inspecting officer has done or omitted to do under this\nDivision.\n\nStored communications  Schedule 1\nPrincipal amendments  Part 1\n\nTelecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   37\n\n(3) Subject to section 155 of this Act, subsections 35(2), (3), (4) and\n(8) of the Ombudsman Act 1976 apply for the purposes of this\nDivision and so apply as if:\n\n(a) a reference in those subsections to an officer were a reference\nto an inspecting officer; and\n\n(b) a reference in those subsections to information did not\ninclude a reference to lawfully accessed information or\nlawfully intercepted information; and\n\n(c) a reference in those subsections to that Act were a reference\nto this Division; and\n\n(d) paragraph 35(3)(b) of that Act were omitted; and\n\n(e) section 35A of that Act had not been enacted.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Section 11A of the Ombudsman Act 1976 does not apply in\nrelation to the exercise or proposed exercise of a power, or the\nperformance or the proposed performance of a function, of the\nOmbudsman under this Division.\n\n(2) A reference in section 19 of the Ombudsman Act 1976 to the\nOmbudsman’s operations does not include a reference to anything\nthat an inspecting officer has done or omitted to do under this\nDivision.\n\nStored communications  Schedule 1\nPrincipal amendments  Part 1\n\nTelecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   37\n\n(3) Subject to section 155 of this Act, subsections 35(2), (3), (4) and\n(8) of the Ombudsman Act 1976 apply for the purposes of this\nDivision and so apply as if:\n\n(a) a reference in those subsections to an officer were a reference\nto an inspecting officer; and\n\n(b) a reference in those subsections to information did not\ninclude a reference to lawfully accessed information or\nlawfully intercepted information; and\n\n(c) a reference in those subsections to that Act were a reference\nto this Division; and\n\n(d) paragraph 35(3)(b) of that Act were omitted; and\n\n(e) section 35A of that Act had not been enacted.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-157-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-157-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-157-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-157-ss-8"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "054ae3842849f122f9c9d4a7cb41844fd135d74d7b61241bf41d83ee1582293e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-157",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "157 Application of Ombudsman Act",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 40,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Section 11A of the Ombudsman Act 1976 does not apply in\nrelation to the exercise or proposed exercise of a power, or the\nperformance or the proposed performance of a function, of the\nOmbudsman under this Division.\n\n(2) A reference in section 19 of the Ombudsman Act 1976 to the\nOmbudsman’s operations does not include a reference to anything\nthat an inspecting officer has done or omitted to do under this\nDivision.\n\nStored communications  Schedule 1\nPrincipal amendments  Part 1\n\nTelecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   37\n\n(3) Subject to section 155 of this Act, subsections 35(2), (3), (4) and\n(8) of the Ombudsman Act 1976 apply for the purposes of this\nDivision and so apply as if:\n\n(a) a reference in those subsections to an officer were a reference\nto an inspecting officer; and\n\n(b) a reference in those subsections to information did not\ninclude a reference to lawfully accessed information or\nlawfully intercepted information; and\n\n(c) a reference in those subsections to that Act were a reference\nto this Division; and\n\n(d) paragraph 35(3)(b) of that Act were omitted; and\n\n(e) section 35A of that Act had not been enacted."
    },
