    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-158",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "158 Exchange of information between Ombudsman and State",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-158"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.41",
      "values:originalText": "inspecting authorities\n\n(1) The Ombudsman may give information that:\n\n(a) relates to an enforcement agency that is an authority of a\nState (a State agency); and\n\n(b) was obtained by the Ombudsman under this Act;\nto the authority (a State inspecting authority) that, under the law of\nthe State concerned, has the function of making inspections of the\nkind referred to in paragraph 35(1)(h) in relation to the agency.\n\n(2) The Ombudsman may give information to an authority under\nsubsection (1) only if the Ombudsman is satisfied that the giving of\nthe information is necessary to enable the authority to perform its\nfunctions in relation to the State agency.\n\n(3) The Ombudsman may receive from a State inspecting authority\ninformation relevant to the performance of the Ombudsman’s\nfunctions under this Act.\n\nSchedule 1  Stored communications",
      "skos:definition": "inspecting authorities\n\n(1) The Ombudsman may give information that:\n\n(a) relates to an enforcement agency that is an authority of a\nState (a State agency); and\n\n(b) was obtained by the Ombudsman under this Act;\nto the authority (a State inspecting authority) that, under the law of\nthe State concerned, has the function of making inspections of the\nkind referred to in paragraph 35(1)(h) in relation to the agency.\n\n(2) The Ombudsman may give information to an authority under\nsubsection (1) only if the Ombudsman is satisfied that the giving of\nthe information is necessary to enable the authority to perform its\nfunctions in relation to the State agency.\n\n(3) The Ombudsman may receive from a State inspecting authority\ninformation relevant to the performance of the Ombudsman’s\nfunctions under this Act.\n\nSchedule 1  Stored communications",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-158-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-158-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-158-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "516548d0cfde581deae940307cc8454dbb916b4cc2940cc91b4c9f8de1a1586b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-158",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "158 Exchange of information between Ombudsman and State",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 41,
      "values:originalText": "inspecting authorities\n\n(1) The Ombudsman may give information that:\n\n(a) relates to an enforcement agency that is an authority of a\nState (a State agency); and\n\n(b) was obtained by the Ombudsman under this Act;\nto the authority (a State inspecting authority) that, under the law of\nthe State concerned, has the function of making inspections of the\nkind referred to in paragraph 35(1)(h) in relation to the agency.\n\n(2) The Ombudsman may give information to an authority under\nsubsection (1) only if the Ombudsman is satisfied that the giving of\nthe information is necessary to enable the authority to perform its\nfunctions in relation to the State agency.\n\n(3) The Ombudsman may receive from a State inspecting authority\ninformation relevant to the performance of the Ombudsman’s\nfunctions under this Act.\n\nSchedule 1  Stored communications"
    },
