      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-42-ss-7-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-42-ss-7-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "08c6feb8f3d3163dded1335677f785d199c669bc730ffe74ed251628f345578d",
      "skos:note": "Access or communication of information is unlawful without court order."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-42-ss-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "42(7) Telecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 46,
      "values:originalText": "(7) Without limiting the orders that may be made under this section\nagainst a person (the defendant) in respect of a particular access to\nor a particular communication of information, a court may make an\norder of one or more of the following kinds:\n\n(a) an order declaring the access or communication, as the case\nrequires, to have been unlawful;\n\n(b) an order that the defendant pay to the aggrieved person such\ndamages as the court considers appropriate;\n\n(c) an order in the nature of an injunction (including a mandatory\ninjunction);\n\n(d) an order that the defendant pay to the aggrieved person an\namount not exceeding the amount that, in the opinion of the\ncourt, represents the total gross income derived by the\ndefendant as a result of the access or communication, as the\ncase requires.\nTerms etc. of orders"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-42-ss-7-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
