      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.46",
      "values:originalText": "(8) Without limiting the orders that may be made by a court under this\nsection, an order may:\n\n(a) include such provisions as the court considers necessary for\nthe purposes of the order; and\n\n(b) be made either unconditionally or subject to such terms and\nconditions as the court determines.\n\nStored communications  Schedule 1\nPrincipal amendments  Part 1\n\nTelecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   43\nInjunctive relief—variation etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(8) Without limiting the orders that may be made by a court under this\nsection, an order may:\n\n(a) include such provisions as the court considers necessary for\nthe purposes of the order; and\n\n(b) be made either unconditionally or subject to such terms and\nconditions as the court determines.\n\nStored communications  Schedule 1\nPrincipal amendments  Part 1\n\nTelecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   43\nInjunctive relief—variation etc.",
