    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-42-ss-11",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "42(11) Telecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-42-ss-11"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.46",
      "values:originalText": "(11) Despite subsection (1) of this section, this section does not apply to\nan accessing that contravenes subsection 108(1) only because of a\ndefect or irregularity (other than a substantial defect or\nirregularity):\n\n(a) in, or in connection with the issue of, a document purporting\nto be a warrant; or\n\n(b) in connection with the execution of a warrant, or the\npurported execution of a document purporting to be a\nwarrant.",
      "skos:definition": "(11) Despite subsection (1) of this section, this section does not apply to\nan accessing that contravenes subsection 108(1) only because of a\ndefect or irregularity (other than a substantial defect or\nirregularity):\n\n(a) in, or in connection with the issue of, a document purporting\nto be a warrant; or\n\n(b) in connection with the execution of a warrant, or the\npurported execution of a document purporting to be a\nwarrant.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-42"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-42-ss-11-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-1-sec-42-ss-11-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "195fc603ea8cd7d5f1b37e8fc61ff410bf8f2dc02e8210b68bb5b0f5c0609cb5",
      "skos:note": "Exemptions from interception for issuing or executing a warrant"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-1-sec-42-ss-11",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "42(11) Telecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 46,
      "values:originalText": "(11) Despite subsection (1) of this section, this section does not apply to\nan accessing that contravenes subsection 108(1) only because of a\ndefect or irregularity (other than a substantial defect or\nirregularity):\n\n(a) in, or in connection with the issue of, a document purporting\nto be a warrant; or\n\n(b) in connection with the execution of a warrant, or the\npurported execution of a document purporting to be a\nwarrant."
    },
