    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-3-sec-9",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "9 Subsection 11B(1)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-3-sec-9"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.74",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1) The Attorney-General may, under his or her hand, issue a warrant\nin respect of a person if:\n\n(a) the Director-General of Security gives a notice in writing to\nthe Attorney-General requesting the Attorney-General to\nissue a warrant under this section authorising persons\napproved under section 12 in respect of the warrant to do acts\nor things referred to in subsection 9A(1A) in relation to:\n\nEquipment-based interception  Schedule 3\n\nTelecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   71\n\n(i) communications that are being made to or from any\ntelecommunications service that a person or foreign\norganisation is using, or is likely to use; or\n\n(ii) communications that are being made by means of a\nparticular telecommunications device that a person or\nforeign organisation is using, or is likely to use;\n\nfor the purpose of obtaining foreign intelligence relating to a\nmatter specified in the notice; and\n\n(b) the Attorney-General is satisfied, on the basis of advice\nreceived from the relevant Minister, that:\n\n(i) the obtaining of foreign intelligence relating to that\nmatter is important in relation to the defence of the\nCommonwealth or to the conduct of the\nCommonwealth’s international affairs; and\n\n(ii) it is necessary to intercept the communications of the\nperson or foreign organisation in order to obtain the\nintelligence referred to in paragraph (a); and\n\n(iii) relying on a telecommunications service warrant to\nobtain the intelligence would be ineffective.\n\n(1A) The warrant authorises persons approved under section 12 in\nrespect of the warrant to intercept, subject to any conditions or\nrestrictions that are specified in the warrant:\n\n(a) communications that are being made to or from any\ntelecommunications service that the person or foreign\norganisation is using, or is likely to use; or\n\n(b) communications that are being made by means of a\ntelecommunications device, identified in the warrant, that the\nperson or foreign organisation is using, or is likely to use.\nNote:\nSubsection (3) restricts the issuing of a warrant authorising\ninterception of communications made by means of a\ntelecommunications device identified in the warrant.\n\n(1B) The warrant may authorise entry on any premises specified in the\nwarrant for the purpose of installing, maintaining, using or\nrecovering any equipment used to intercept such communications.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1) The Attorney-General may, under his or her hand, issue a warrant\nin respect of a person if:\n\n(a) the Director-General of Security gives a notice in writing to\nthe Attorney-General requesting the Attorney-General to\nissue a warrant under this section authorising persons\napproved under section 12 in respect of the warrant to do acts\nor things referred to in subsection 9A(1A) in relation to:\n\nEquipment-based interception  Schedule 3\n\nTelecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   71\n\n(i) communications that are being made to or from any\ntelecommunications service that a person or foreign\norganisation is using, or is likely to use; or\n\n(ii) communications that are being made by means of a\nparticular telecommunications device that a person or\nforeign organisation is using, or is likely to use;\n\nfor the purpose of obtaining foreign intelligence relating to a\nmatter specified in the notice; and\n\n(b) the Attorney-General is satisfied, on the basis of advice\nreceived from the relevant Minister, that:\n\n(i) the obtaining of foreign intelligence relating to that\nmatter is important in relation to the defence of the\nCommonwealth or to the conduct of the\nCommonwealth’s international affairs; and\n\n(ii) it is necessary to intercept the communications of the\nperson or foreign organisation in order to obtain the\nintelligence referred to in paragraph (a); and\n\n(iii) relying on a telecommunications service warrant to\nobtain the intelligence would be ineffective.\n\n(1A) The warrant authorises persons approved under section 12 in\nrespect of the warrant to intercept, subject to any conditions or\nrestrictions that are specified in the warrant:\n\n(a) communications that are being made to or from any\ntelecommunications service that the person or foreign\norganisation is using, or is likely to use; or\n\n(b) communications that are being made by means of a\ntelecommunications device, identified in the warrant, that the\nperson or foreig",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-3-sec-9-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-3-sec-9-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-3-sec-9-ss-1b"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fc61fc4a50e655d12b70c909f99174b3a8932dca19bfcf9d8128e3cad72db45b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-3-sec-9",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9 Subsection 11B(1)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 74,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1) The Attorney-General may, under his or her hand, issue a warrant\nin respect of a person if:\n\n(a) the Director-General of Security gives a notice in writing to\nthe Attorney-General requesting the Attorney-General to\nissue a warrant under this section authorising persons\napproved under section 12 in respect of the warrant to do acts\nor things referred to in subsection 9A(1A) in relation to:\n\nEquipment-based interception  Schedule 3\n\nTelecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   71\n\n(i) communications that are being made to or from any\ntelecommunications service that a person or foreign\norganisation is using, or is likely to use; or\n\n(ii) communications that are being made by means of a\nparticular telecommunications device that a person or\nforeign organisation is using, or is likely to use;\n\nfor the purpose of obtaining foreign intelligence relating to a\nmatter specified in the notice; and\n\n(b) the Attorney-General is satisfied, on the basis of advice\nreceived from the relevant Minister, that:\n\n(i) the obtaining of foreign intelligence relating to that\nmatter is important in relation to the defence of the\nCommonwealth or to the conduct of the\nCommonwealth’s international affairs; and\n\n(ii) it is necessary to intercept the communications of the\nperson or foreign organisation in order to obtain the\nintelligence referred to in paragraph (a); and\n\n(iii) relying on a telecommunications service warrant to\nobtain the intelligence would be ineffective.\n\n(1A) The warrant authorises persons approved under section 12 in\nrespect of the warrant to intercept, subject to any conditions or\nrestrictions that are specified in the warrant:\n\n(a) communications that are being made to or from any\ntelecommunications service that the person or foreign\norganisation is using, or is likely to use; or\n\n(b) communications that are being made by means of a\ntelecommunications device, identified in the warrant, that the\nperson or foreign organisation is using, or is likely to use.\nNote:\nSubsection (3) restricts the issuing of a warrant authorising\ninterception of communications made by means of a\ntelecommunications device identified in the warrant.\n\n(1B) The warrant may authorise entry on any premises specified in the\nwarrant for the purpose of installing, maintaining, using or\nrecovering any equipment used to intercept such communications."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-3-sec-9-ss-1",
