      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.74",
      "values:originalText": "(1A) The warrant authorises persons approved under section 12 in\nrespect of the warrant to intercept, subject to any conditions or\nrestrictions that are specified in the warrant:\n\n(a) communications that are being made to or from any\ntelecommunications service that the person or foreign\norganisation is using, or is likely to use; or\n\n(b) communications that are being made by means of a\ntelecommunications device, identified in the warrant, that the\nperson or foreign organisation is using, or is likely to use.\nNote:\nSubsection (3) restricts the issuing of a warrant authorising\ninterception of communications made by means of a\ntelecommunications device identified in the warrant.",
      "skos:definition": "(1A) The warrant authorises persons approved under section 12 in\nrespect of the warrant to intercept, subject to any conditions or\nrestrictions that are specified in the warrant:\n\n(a) communications that are being made to or from any\ntelecommunications service that the person or foreign\norganisation is using, or is likely to use; or\n\n(b) communications that are being made by means of a\ntelecommunications device, identified in the warrant, that the\nperson or foreign organisation is using, or is likely to use.\nNote:\nSubsection (3) restricts the issuing of a warrant authorising\ninterception of communications made by means of a\ntelecommunications device identified in the warrant.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-3-sec-9"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-3-sec-9-ss-1a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-3-sec-9-ss-1a-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-3-sec-9-ss-1a-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "04c0704898add688faa38b36bef400c457a17f405133a4e25022edf2afeaf4f3",
      "skos:note": "Authorises interception of communications under specified conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-3-sec-9-ss-1a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "9(1A) Subsection 11B(1)",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 74,
      "values:originalText": "(1A) The warrant authorises persons approved under section 12 in\nrespect of the warrant to intercept, subject to any conditions or\nrestrictions that are specified in the warrant:\n\n(a) communications that are being made to or from any\ntelecommunications service that the person or foreign\norganisation is using, or is likely to use; or\n\n(b) communications that are being made by means of a\ntelecommunications device, identified in the warrant, that the\nperson or foreign organisation is using, or is likely to use.\nNote:\nSubsection (3) restricts the issuing of a warrant authorising\ninterception of communications made by means of a\ntelecommunications device identified in the warrant."
    },
