    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-3-sec-20",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20 Paragraph 46A(2)(a)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-3-sec-20"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.78",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the paragraph, substitute:\n\n(a) how much the privacy of any person or persons would be\nlikely to be interfered with by intercepting under a warrant:\n\n(i) communications made to or from any\ntelecommunications service used, or likely to be used,\nby the person in respect of whom the warrant is sought;\nor\n\n(ii) communications made by means of a particular\ntelecommunications device used, or likely to be used, by\nthe person in respect of whom the warrant is sought;\n\nas the case requires; and",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the paragraph, substitute:\n\n(a) how much the privacy of any person or persons would be\nlikely to be interfered with by intercepting under a warrant:\n\n(i) communications made to or from any\ntelecommunications service used, or likely to be used,\nby the person in respect of whom the warrant is sought;\nor\n\n(ii) communications made by means of a particular\ntelecommunications device used, or likely to be used, by\nthe person in respect of whom the warrant is sought;\n\nas the case requires; and",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-3-sec-20-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "50df18e4a178db7b138ffba8af5ace56e87489663403309791500851fe2966f3",
      "skos:note": "Specify the scope of interception under a warrant"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-3-sec-20",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20 Paragraph 46A(2)(a)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 78,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the paragraph, substitute:\n\n(a) how much the privacy of any person or persons would be\nlikely to be interfered with by intercepting under a warrant:\n\n(i) communications made to or from any\ntelecommunications service used, or likely to be used,\nby the person in respect of whom the warrant is sought;\nor\n\n(ii) communications made by means of a particular\ntelecommunications device used, or likely to be used, by\nthe person in respect of whom the warrant is sought;\n\nas the case requires; and"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-3-sec-20-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-3-sec-20"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-3-sec-21",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21 At the end of section 46A",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-3-sec-21"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.78",
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\n(3) The Judge or nominated AAT member must not issue a warrant\nthat authorises interception of communications made by means of a\ntelecommunications device identified in the warrant unless he or\nshe is satisfied that:\n\n(a) there are no other practicable methods available to the agency\nat the time of making the application to identify the\ntelecommunications services used, or likely to be used, by\nthe person in respect of whom the warrant would be issued;\nor\n\n(b) interception of communications made to or from a\ntelecommunications service used, or likely to be used, by that\nperson would not otherwise be practicable.",
      "skos:definition": "Add:\n\n(3) The Judge or nominated AAT member must not issue a warrant\nthat authorises interception of communications made by means of a\ntelecommunications device identified in the warrant unless he or\nshe is satisfied that:\n\n(a) there are no other practicable methods available to the agency\nat the time of making the application to identify the\ntelecommunications services used, or likely to be used, by\nthe person in respect of whom the warrant would be issued;\nor\n\n(b) interception of communications made to or from a\ntelecommunications service used, or likely to be used, by that\nperson would not otherwise be practicable.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-3-sec-21-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-3-sec-21-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-3-sec-21-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-3-sec-21-logic-alleninterval-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8beaa7f9a8c6821aeefd5a5a9e8caf0918105d39cb01057e87aaf9a44badf6e9",
      "skos:note": "Must not issue warrant for interception of communications without certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-3-sec-21",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21 At the end of section 46A",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 78,
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\n(3) The Judge or nominated AAT member must not issue a warrant\nthat authorises interception of communications made by means of a\ntelecommunications device identified in the warrant unless he or\nshe is satisfied that:\n\n(a) there are no other practicable methods available to the agency\nat the time of making the application to identify the\ntelecommunications services used, or likely to be used, by\nthe person in respect of whom the warrant would be issued;\nor\n\n(b) interception of communications made to or from a\ntelecommunications service used, or likely to be used, by that\nperson would not otherwise be practicable."
    },
