    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-4-sec-7",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "7 Subsection 5D(1)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-4-sec-7"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.80",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\nGeneral types of serious offences\n\n(1) An offence is a serious offence if it is:\n\n(a) a murder, or an offence of a kind equivalent to murder; or\n\nClass 1 and class 2 offences  Schedule 4\nAmendments  Part 1\n\nTelecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   77\n\n(b) a kidnapping, or an offence of a kind equivalent to\nkidnapping; or\n\n(c) an offence against Division 307 of the Criminal Code; or\n\n(d) an offence constituted by conduct involving an act or acts of\nterrorism; or\n\n(e) an offence against Division 72, 101, 102 or 103 of the\nCriminal Code; or\n\n(f) except for the purposes of an application for a warrant by an\nagency other than the ACC, an offence in relation to which\nthe ACC is conducting a special investigation.\nNote:\nThe heading to section 5D is replaced by the heading “Serious offences”.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\nGeneral types of serious offences\n\n(1) An offence is a serious offence if it is:\n\n(a) a murder, or an offence of a kind equivalent to murder; or\n\nClass 1 and class 2 offences  Schedule 4\nAmendments  Part 1\n\nTelecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   77\n\n(b) a kidnapping, or an offence of a kind equivalent to\nkidnapping; or\n\n(c) an offence against Division 307 of the Criminal Code; or\n\n(d) an offence constituted by conduct involving an act or acts of\nterrorism; or\n\n(e) an offence against Division 72, 101, 102 or 103 of the\nCriminal Code; or\n\n(f) except for the purposes of an application for a warrant by an\nagency other than the ACC, an offence in relation to which\nthe ACC is conducting a special investigation.\nNote:\nThe heading to section 5D is replaced by the heading “Serious offences”.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-4-sec-7-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-4-sec-7-logic-alleninterval-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-4-sec-7-logic-ltl-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-4-sec-7-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-4-sec-7-logic-deontic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7bc5e1c7edf92ee7628bb5459a37ce47b17f2f7e229ef1439bb4a4b4b27d9eff",
      "skos:note": "Defines serious offences"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-4-sec-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "7 Subsection 5D(1)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 80,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\nGeneral types of serious offences\n\n(1) An offence is a serious offence if it is:\n\n(a) a murder, or an offence of a kind equivalent to murder; or\n\nClass 1 and class 2 offences  Schedule 4\nAmendments  Part 1\n\nTelecommunications (Interception) Amendment Act 2006                   77\n\n(b) a kidnapping, or an offence of a kind equivalent to\nkidnapping; or\n\n(c) an offence against Division 307 of the Criminal Code; or\n\n(d) an offence constituted by conduct involving an act or acts of\nterrorism; or\n\n(e) an offence against Division 72, 101, 102 or 103 of the\nCriminal Code; or\n\n(f) except for the purposes of an application for a warrant by an\nagency other than the ACC, an offence in relation to which\nthe ACC is conducting a special investigation.\nNote:\nThe heading to section 5D is replaced by the heading “Serious offences”."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-4-sec-7-norm",
