      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.81",
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\n(7) An offence is also a serious offence if it is an offence constituted\nby receiving or assisting a person who is, to the offender’s\nknowledge, guilty of a serious offence mentioned in subsection (1),\n\nSchedule 4  Class 1 and class 2 offences",
      "skos:definition": "Add:\n\n(7) An offence is also a serious offence if it is an offence constituted\nby receiving or assisting a person who is, to the offender’s\nknowledge, guilty of a serious offence mentioned in subsection (1),\n\nSchedule 4  Class 1 and class 2 offences",
