    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-5-sec-11",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "11 Subsections 57(1) and (2)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-5-sec-11"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.87",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\n\n(1) The chief officer of an agency must, on being satisfied that the\ngrounds on which a warrant was issued to the agency have ceased\nto exist:\n\n(a) cause the Secretary of the Department to be informed\nforthwith that the chief officer proposes to revoke the\nwarrant; and\n\n(b) cause the chief officer of any other agency that is exercising\nauthority under the warrant to be informed forthwith of the\nproposed revocation of the warrant; and\n\n(c) by writing signed by him or her, revoke the warrant.\n\n(2) The chief officer of an agency may at any time, by writing signed\nby him or her, revoke a warrant issued to the agency after:\n\n(a) causing the Secretary of the Department to be informed of\nthe proposed revocation; and\n\n(b) causing the chief officer of any other agency that is\nexercising authority under the warrant to be informed\n\nSchedule 5  Transfer of functions",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\n\n(1) The chief officer of an agency must, on being satisfied that the\ngrounds on which a warrant was issued to the agency have ceased\nto exist:\n\n(a) cause the Secretary of the Department to be informed\nforthwith that the chief officer proposes to revoke the\nwarrant; and\n\n(b) cause the chief officer of any other agency that is exercising\nauthority under the warrant to be informed forthwith of the\nproposed revocation of the warrant; and\n\n(c) by writing signed by him or her, revoke the warrant.\n\n(2) The chief officer of an agency may at any time, by writing signed\nby him or her, revoke a warrant issued to the agency after:\n\n(a) causing the Secretary of the Department to be informed of\nthe proposed revocation; and\n\n(b) causing the chief officer of any other agency that is\nexercising authority under the warrant to be informed\n\nSchedule 5  Transfer of functions",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-5-sec-11-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-5-sec-11-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "45006b563b2fa2182b7ea81cca2aac16faa404d7946d1c0f51f91fbff6cf069d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-5-sec-11",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "11 Subsections 57(1) and (2)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 87,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\n\n(1) The chief officer of an agency must, on being satisfied that the\ngrounds on which a warrant was issued to the agency have ceased\nto exist:\n\n(a) cause the Secretary of the Department to be informed\nforthwith that the chief officer proposes to revoke the\nwarrant; and\n\n(b) cause the chief officer of any other agency that is exercising\nauthority under the warrant to be informed forthwith of the\nproposed revocation of the warrant; and\n\n(c) by writing signed by him or her, revoke the warrant.\n\n(2) The chief officer of an agency may at any time, by writing signed\nby him or her, revoke a warrant issued to the agency after:\n\n(a) causing the Secretary of the Department to be informed of\nthe proposed revocation; and\n\n(b) causing the chief officer of any other agency that is\nexercising authority under the warrant to be informed\n\nSchedule 5  Transfer of functions"
    },
