    {
      "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-5-sec-80",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "80 Commonwealth agencies to keep documents connected with issue",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-5-sec-80"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006.pdf, p.89",
      "values:originalText": "of warrants\n\nThe chief officer of a Commonwealth agency must cause to be\nkept in the agency’s records:\n\n(a) each warrant issued to the agency; and\n\n(b) a copy of each notification under paragraph 53(1)(b) of the\nissue of such a warrant, being a notification given to the\nSecretary of the Department; and\n\n(c) each instrument revoking such a warrant; and\n\n(d) a copy of each certificate issued under subsection 61(4) by a\ncertifying officer of the agency; and\n\n(e) each authorisation by the chief officer under subsection\n66(2).\n\nSchedule 5  Transfer of functions",
      "skos:definition": "of warrants\n\nThe chief officer of a Commonwealth agency must cause to be\nkept in the agency’s records:\n\n(a) each warrant issued to the agency; and\n\n(b) a copy of each notification under paragraph 53(1)(b) of the\nissue of such a warrant, being a notification given to the\nSecretary of the Department; and\n\n(c) each instrument revoking such a warrant; and\n\n(d) a copy of each certificate issued under subsection 61(4) by a\ncertifying officer of the agency; and\n\n(e) each authorisation by the chief officer under subsection\n66(2).\n\nSchedule 5  Transfer of functions",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-5-sec-80-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006-sch-5-sec-80-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "674d83448c8fcdcc27aa9cc22b6a9a4e8adf9b0f986be034a4962b02ec4662be",
      "skos:note": "Keep documents connected with issue of warrants",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/telecommunications-interception-amendment-act-2006#sch-5-sec-80",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "80 Commonwealth agencies to keep documents connected with issue",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 89,
      "values:originalText": "of warrants\n\nThe chief officer of a Commonwealth agency must cause to be\nkept in the agency’s records:\n\n(a) each warrant issued to the agency; and\n\n(b) a copy of each notification under paragraph 53(1)(b) of the\nissue of such a warrant, being a notification given to the\nSecretary of the Department; and\n\n(c) each instrument revoking such a warrant; and\n\n(d) a copy of each certificate issued under subsection 61(4) by a\ncertifying officer of the agency; and\n\n(e) each authorisation by the chief officer under subsection\n66(2).\n\nSchedule 5  Transfer of functions"
    },
